ulated item to a prohibited buyer after checking convincing fake papers. The clerk and owner are both convicted. Which theories are needed?","answer":"Strict liability for the clerk and vicarious liability for the owner."},{"drill_type":"cut","target_skill":"one-box answer detection","prompt":"Why is ''strict liability only'' incomplete when both clerk and owner are convicted?","answer":"It explains the clerk but not the owner."},{"drill_type":"cut","target_skill":"false compromise detection","prompt":"Why is ''either strict or vicarious liability'' wrong when the result convicts both actors?","answer":"The result requires both theories, not either one."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
