       tension_point = 'second-degree implied-malice common-law murder vs third-degree felony murder',
       fact_pattern = 'A statute in the jurisdiction defines murder in the first degree as knowingly killing another person after deliberation. Deliberation is defined as “cool reflection for any length of time no matter how brief.” Murder in the second degree is defined as all other murder at common law except felony murder. Felony murder is murder in the third degree. Manslaughter is defined by the common law.

At 2 a.m., Paul held up Martha’s private all-night Christian bookstore, The Lampstand, using an assault rifle. During the holdup, two police cars with flashing lights drove up in front of the store. To create a situation in which the police would hesitate to enter, and thus give Paul a chance to escape out the back, Paul fired several rounds through the front window of the store. Paul then ran out the back, but upon discovering another police car there, surrendered quietly. One of the shots he fired while in the store struck and killed Stephen, who was stealing supplies from Daniel’s closed copy shop across the street.

The most serious degree of criminal homicide Paul is guilty of is:',
       question_stem = 'A statute in the jurisdiction defines murder in the first degree as knowingly killing another person after deliberation. Deliberation is defined as “cool reflection for any length of time no matter how brief.” Murder in the second degree is defined as all other murder at common law except felony murder. Felony murder is murder in the third degree. Manslaughter is defined by the common law.

At 2 a.m., Paul held up Martha’s private all-night Christian bookstore, The Lampstand, using an assault rifle. During the holdup, two police cars with flashing lights drove up in front of the store. To create a situation in which the police would hesitate to enter, and thus give Paul a chance to escape out the back, Paul fired several rounds through the front window of the store. Paul then ran out the back, but upon discovering another police car there, surrendered quietly. One of the shots he fired while in the store struck and killed Stephen, who was stealing supplies from Daniel’s closed copy shop across the street.

The most serious degree of criminal homicide Paul is guilty of is:

Call: most serious degree of criminal homicide.

Prediction: Start at the top and move down. First-degree needs knowingly killing after deliberation. If that fails, ask whether the facts still create common-law murder. If yes, B beats C because C is only third-degree felony murder.',
       call_of_question = 'Call: most serious degree of criminal homicide.

