 the statutory ladder and pick the highest surviving degree.","type":"answer_array","trigger":"Answer choices are homicide degrees, and the call says most serious.","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true},{"id":"SK-CRIMINAL-ACT-VS-KILL-02","statement":"Separate deliberate dangerous conduct from a knowing killing of this victim. Deliberating before firing does not automatically satisfy a statute requiring knowingly killing another person.","type":"trap_spotting","trigger":"The statute uses knowing killing; the facts show a deliberate risky act with an unintended victim.","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true}],"drill_seeds":[{"drill_type":"ladder_ranking","target_skill":"Most-serious-degree call","prompt":"A defendant is guilty of both felony murder and implied-malice murder; the statute ranks implied-malice murder higher. Which degree controls?","answer":"The higher surviving degree controls."},{"drill_type":"trap_spotting","target_skill":"True lower degree","prompt":"Why can felony murder be wrong even if the killing occurred during a felony?","answer":"Because the call asks for the most serious degree, and a higher common-law murder degree may fit."},{"drill_type":"mental_state_split","target_skill":"Act intent vs result intent","prompt":"A defendant deliberately fires a gun but does not know the actual victim is present. What first-degree element should you check?","answer":"Whether the defendant knowingly killed another person after deliberation."},{"drill_type":"gold_key_recall","target_skill":"Reckless-indifference murder","prompt":"What homicide anchor is triggered by firing several rifle rounds through a front window toward an area where people are present?","answer":"Extreme reckless indifference can supply common-law murder malice."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
