       why_wrong_or_correct = 'B is correct. Paul intentionally fired multiple rifle rounds through the front window of an occupied commercial setting while police were outside. That conduct creates a grave, obvious risk to human life. The killing therefore fits common-law murder through implied malice / depraved-heart malice, even though Paul did not knowingly kill Stephen after deliberation.

