       why_attractive = NULL,
       why_wrong_or_correct = 'A is correct. Gold Key: extreme recklessness plus foreseeable death can supply murder liability even when the defendant did not personally shoot the victim and did not specifically intend that victim’s death. Silver Key: in a “guilty/not guilty because X” array, the reason matters. The right guilty answer is not just “guilty”; it must give the right route to guilt.

Paul knowingly used Timothy’s jealousy and violent temper to send him armed into a guarded office. That created a grave and foreseeable risk that Timothy or someone else would be shot. John’s shooting did not erase Paul’s causal role because the guard’s response was the kind of foreseeable consequence Paul set in motion.',
