       why_attractive = 'When a student isn''t sure whether poison or premeditation alone is sufficient, the ''both'' answer looks safer and more comprehensive.',
       why_wrong_or_correct = 'Compound of A and B. ''Both poison AND premeditation'' fails because neither prong is satisfied. Even if one were, the absence of malice aforethought means no murder to elevate.',
       future_cue = 'Both prongs fail independently (see A and B recovery). Also: no malice aforethought means there is no murder for these aggravators to elevate. The ''compound'' answer is doubly wrong.',
