Of which crime is Lydia most likely guilty?

The original row is BARMATRIX Q# 19263, a Criminal Law and Procedure / Property Crimes item keyed to false pretenses.',
       question_stem = 'At a private Christian music expo, Lydia tells Paul, a collector of antique chapel handbell sets, that she is the purchasing manager for a well-known Christian retreat center and is buying seven handbell sets for its chapel choir. Relying on that statement, Paul signs bills of sale transferring ownership of all seven sets to Lydia and accepts Lydia’s personal check. Lydia is not affiliated with the retreat center, the check is drawn on a closed account, and she has no intention of paying. She loads the handbells into her van and leaves with the signed bills of sale.

Of which crime is Lydia most likely guilty?

The original row is BARMATRIX Q# 19263, a Criminal Law and Procedure / Property Crimes item keyed to false pretenses.

Predict before choices: this is not “was there fraud?” It is “which theft label fits the transfer?” The fact to hunt is what Paul transferred.

Prediction: if ownership/title moved because of a present-fact lie, the crime is false pretenses.',
       call_of_question = 'Predict before choices: this is not “was there fraud?” It is “which theft label fits the transfer?” The fact to hunt is what Paul transferred.

