efore checking formalities.","type":"answer_array","trigger":"Choice set includes the role-holder, the grantor, and the organization as possible owners.","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true}],"drill_seeds":[{"drill_type":"anchor_recall","target_skill":"ascertainable grantee by role","prompt":"A deed says “to the choir director of a school today.” One person held that role at delivery. Who is the grantee?","answer":"The role-holder."},{"drill_type":"cut","target_skill":"fabricated deed formalities","prompt":"Cut the choice: “Grantor keeps title because the grantee did not sign the deed.”","answer":"NOT_TRUE; fabricated_rule; grantee signature generally not required."},{"drill_type":"answer_array","target_skill":"role-holder vs entity","prompt":"A deed says “to the treasurer of Mercy Hall.” Does that automatically make Mercy Hall the grantee?","answer":"No; first ask who the role-holder was."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
