       question_stem = 'Barnabas owns a privately run Bible-story mini-golf course called The Exodus Course. He sells it to Ruth. The sale contract says that Ruth buys the course "as is, including all hidden subsurface drainage defects, whether known or unknown." Both Barnabas and Ruth believe the underground drainage tunnels beneath the "Red Sea Crossing" hole are intact. Before signing, however, those tunnels had already collapsed from storm erosion. Ruth later discovers the collapse and seeks rescission for mutual mistake. How should the court rule?

How should the court rule?',
       call_of_question = 'How should the court rule?',
       difficulty = 2,
       metadata = '{"source_file":"CQ20351.md","source_question_id":"20351","variant_slug":"red_sea_mini_golf","batch":"cq-updated-copy-2026-06-20","outline_code":"54030600","outline_code_verified":true,"difficulty_band":"trap repair","deciding_phase":"CUT","confidence":"ANCHOR_ASSISTED","splitting_fact":null,"distilled_core_question":"Buyer signs an as-is clause covering hidden unknown defects. Both parties are wrong about a hidden preexisting defect. Buyer seeks mutual-mistake rescission. Who wins?","review_truth":"A mutual mistake does not support rescission when the contract assigned that mistake-risk to the party seeking rescission.","dominant_trap":"C","anchor_card":{"card_id":"REM-CONTRACTS-RISK-BEFORE-RESCISSION-01","title":"Risk before rescission","signal":"Mutual mistake plus as-is / unknown-defect clause.","student_move":"Do not stop at both mistaken. Ask who took the risk.","tiny_rule":"If the claimant accepted the mistake-risk, rescission is denied.","trap":"Picking the mutual-mistake-only grant answer.","confidence":"ANCHOR_ASSISTED"},"gold_keys":[{"id":"GK-CONTRACTS-AS-IS-MISTAKE-01","statement":"A mutual mistake does not support rescission if the party seeking rescission bore the risk. An as-is clause can allocate unknown hidden-defect risk to that party.","type":"rule","trigger":"A mutual mistake stem plus an express as-is or unknown-defect risk-allocation term.","authority":"Restatement (Second) of Contracts §§ 152, 154.","last_minute_review":true}],"silver_keys":[{"id":"SK-CONTRACTS-AS-IS-MISTAKE-01","statement":"In a grant/deny rescission matrix, separate the mistake fact from the risk-allocation fact. The answer that engages the explicit risk term beats the answer that only says both parties were mistaken.","type":"answer_array","trigger":"Two choices grant rescission, two deny; one denial tracks the as-is clause.","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true}],"drill_seeds":[{"drill_type":"CUT","target_skill":"Overclaim detection","prompt":"Hidden defects are always outside an as-is clause.","answer":"Cut: tiered_absolute."},{"drill_type":"CUT","target_skill":"Fabricated rule detection","prompt":"Deny rescission only if the buyer inspected every hidden component personally.","answer":"Cut: fabricated_rule."},{"drill_type":"ANCHOR","target_skill":"Risk allocation in mutual mistake","prompt":"Both parties were mistaken, but the buyer agreed to take unknown hidden-defect risk. Rescission?","answer":"No rescission."},{"drill_type":"ANSWER_ARRAY","target_skill":"2x2 grant/deny matrix","prompt":"Two choices grant because of mistake; two deny because of risk or a proof condition. Which axis decides?","answer":"Risk allocation."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
