L-01","statement":"Lock the named defendant before reading the added facts: the winning fact must create liability for Lydia, not for Barnabas or the product chain.","type":"cut","trigger":"one defendant named in the call, but choices mention product defect, contractor conduct, and customer payment","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true}],"drill_seeds":[{"drill_type":"CUT","target_skill":"named-defendant filtering","prompt":"Premises owner is sued; one choice says the contractor was careful. Cut or keep?","answer":"Cut as NOT_RESPONSIVE unless it supplies owner breach."},{"drill_type":"CUT","target_skill":"wrong_frame detection","prompt":"Premises owner is sued; one choice says the device had a manufacturing defect. What is the trap?","answer":"Product frame; it needs seller status or owner-discoverability."},{"drill_type":"ANCHOR","target_skill":"invitee inspection duty","prompt":"What owner-side fact most supports an invitee premises claim?","answer":"The owner knew or reasonable inspection would have discovered the dangerous condition."},{"drill_type":"CALIBRATION","target_skill":"anchor-assisted clean cut","prompt":"Three choices miss named-defendant breach; one gives reasonable inspection by owner. Confidence?","answer":"ANCHOR_ASSISTED; commit after call/read check."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
