ense.","type":"distinction","trigger":"Plaintiff amends after defendant already failed to raise a known threshold defense.","authority":"Gilmore v. Shearson/American Express, Inc.; State Auto Ins. Co. v. Thomas Landscaping & Constr., Inc.; Gnotec Reftele AB order.","last_minute_review":true}],"silver_keys":[{"id":"SK-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-JURISDICTION-WORD-01","statement":"Match the jurisdiction word to the call before doing doctrine. Personal jurisdiction is defendant-court power; supplemental jurisdiction is subject-matter power over claims.","type":"trap_spotting","trigger":"A choice switches from personal jurisdiction to supplemental jurisdiction.","authority":null,"last_minute_review":true}],"drill_seeds":[{"drill_type":"cut","target_skill":"wrong_frame","prompt":"The call asks whether a late personal-jurisdiction motion should be granted. A choice says the plaintiff must establish supplemental jurisdiction. Cut or keep?","answer":"Cut: NOT_RESPONSIVE / misfit."},{"drill_type":"anchor","target_skill":"Rule 12 waiver","prompt":"A defendant knew all personal-jurisdiction facts and answered without raising PJ. What happens to the PJ defense?","answer":"Waived."},{"drill_type":"anchor","target_skill":"amended complaint no revival","prompt":"Plaintiff later amends only to add damages from the same transaction against the same defendant. Does that automatically revive waived PJ?","answer":"No."},{"drill_type":"trap_spotting","target_skill":"absolute words","prompt":"A choice says every amended complaint restarts all Rule 12 defenses. What is the C3 tell?","answer":"Every/all overclaim plus fabricated Rule 12 reset."}],"updated_copy_source":"C:/FOC/Workspace/Finished/*_updated.md"}'
